    "fact_rationales": {
      "F17": "Elevated erythrocyte sedimentation rate is a non-specific marker of inflammation, but it is more commonly elevated in conditions like Acute Rheumatic Fever and Infective Endocarditis.",
      "F4": "Dyspnea on exertion, orthopnea, and paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnea are more typical of mitral stenosis.",
      "F5": "Recent treatment with streptokinase for suspected prosthetic mitral valve thrombosis is more indicative of prosthetic valve endocarditis.",
      "F6": "Fever and bilateral knee pain are more suggestive of Acute Rheumatic Fever."
